# Superpowers

Before any response or action, including clarifying questions, read and follow `.agents/skills/using-superpowers/SKILL.md`. If there is even a 1% chance a skill in `.agents/skills/` applies, read that skill and follow it exactly. You do not have a choice. Announce "Using [skill] to [purpose]". If a skill has a checklist, create a todo per item.

Before entering plan mode, if you have not already brainstormed, use `.agents/skills/brainstorming/SKILL.md` first.

Process skills come first, then implementation skills. "Let's build X" → brainstorming. "Fix this bug" → systematic-debugging.

These thoughts mean STOP — you are rationalizing: "this is just a simple question", "I need more context first", "let me explore the codebase first", "the skill is overkill", "I'll just do this one thing first", "I remember this skill".

User instructions in `AGENTS.md` take precedence over skills. Only skip a skill when the human partner has explicitly said to.
